name issue_123_v2_allocation_min
describe 100 kbps link with every v2 switch plus audio v2: the encoder is configured at the codec minimum, as libwebrtc's SimulcastRateAllocator does (issue #123)
duration 40s
allocator v2
pacer v2
rtx v2
cc v2
keyframe v2
audio v2
at 0s capacity=100kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
# Second part of #123 (below, "TaskQueuePacedSender"). First part of #123 (roadmap #64): VideoStreamEncoder::UpdateBitrateAllocation, through
# SimulcastRateAllocator::DistributeAllocationToSimulcastLayers, raises the encoder allocation
# to VideoCodec::minBitrate (50 kbps here) while the frame dropper keeps the unraised target
# (about 28 kbps). Without it our encoder target fell to 21 kbps, below the minimum, and the
# dropper let 27 fps through. libwebrtc (compare/webrtc/reference/video/video_stream_encoder.cc
# 1709-1745, 2502; modules/video_coding/utility/simulcast_rate_allocator.cc 94-100) holds the
# encoder target at 50.0 kbps and drops 435 of 1200 frames (parity-data, seed 1).
# Seeds 1-10 with this change: encoder_dropped 150-301 (mean 225; before 138), audio loss
# 11-31 % (mean 24; before 26), concealed 3.3-8.9 % (mean 7.2; before 8.4).
# Second part of #123: with every v2 switch on, the pacer is run as TaskQueuePacedSender runs it (a pass
# only when a packet, a rate or the pause state changes, or when the timer of the last pass is due; the
# early-return branch of ProcessPackets then no longer re-bases the leaky bucket every millisecond).
# libwebrtc's forward-link trace shows the effect: 99 % of its video and RTX packets leave in the same
# millisecond as an audio packet, so the 100 kbps link queue drains for a whole audio period (250 B) before
# the next audio packet, which is 172-216 B. Ours left them 4-19 ms before it, so the 200-290 B packets
# that were accepted filled the queue to its limit and the next audio packet did not fit.
# Seeds 1-10 with both changes: audio loss 0-0.15 % (before 11-31 %), concealed 0.68-0.93 % (before
# 3.3-8.9 %), encoder_dropped 387-516 (before 150-301). libwebrtc (parity-data, 10 seeds): audio loss
# 0.6 %, concealed 0.52 %, encoder_dropped 420, video 31.8 kbps (ours 29-33), RTX 59.7 kbps (ours 26-53).
# What is left: render fps 1.7-3.6 against 6.0 and keyframe requests 2-20 against 3.3 (receive side, #24 and
# #127), RTX volume 36 against 60 kbps.
# Target (issue #123): net.audio_loss_pct within the parity band of libwebrtc's 0.6 %,
# audio.concealed_pct 0.52 %, video.encoder_dropped 420, net.video_kbps 31.8, net.rtx_kbps 59.7,
# video.render_fps 6.0, video.keyframe_requests 3.3.
expect video.encoder_dropped > 300
expect audio.concealed_pct < 2
expect net.audio_loss_pct < 2
